-- K12's simulator: the kind's three shares at theK, at thirteen entries that are letters.
/-
AtFullSide/K12/ShareK12AtTheK.lean: CONDITIONAL: THE ROW IS NOT PAID: on₁, hM, left₃ STAY PREMISES.

Can the hypotheses be met together? BY STATEMENT. `k12_pays_at_theK`: made · h: YES at the named
files (`k12_bud₁_premises_met`, AtFullSide/K12/FirstBudK12.lean). slot₁₂: an entry with that slot
lies (`k12Entry_slot`, AtFullSide/K12/K12Entry.lean, another house's; not imported). E, apart: NO
VALUE OF THE THIRTEEN IS LAID HERE. T: a structure of data; no value is laid here. THE SECOND
STATEMENT: hM: that the filling's text makes a job at the return's ground: not shown to return.
on₁, left₃: at a Ry that holds of nothing, or where ready never returns, they hold for nothing, AND
SO DOES THE FIELD on. NO FAMILY Th IS KNOWN THAT MEETS THEM AT THE RELATION THAT IS TO BE COUNTED
(Ry := the served requests).

A SHARE CAN HOLD FOR NOTHING, AND WHERE IS NO MATTER OF E: G's lists are A.H's sides one for one
(`theGOfReturn_prover`, E2E/TheG.lean), so G has a list of the kind where the maker's prover has a
side at a place of the kind. Where it has none, or where such a list has no seated side in the
description (L.side … = none), pays and bud are over nothing. A list left bare would make pays
false, not empty: pays is proved here under its four premises, so under them no list of the kind
with a seated side is bare at this K. The field on is over nothing also where no part of a test is
called at any run.

What is here. AN ASSEMBLY OF OTHERS' LAWS; NOTHING NEW IS PROVED ON A SIMULATOR. `KindShare` A G
A.H Rel Th .K12 (Honest/Law/RowDebtsByKind.lean: an abbreviation of `KindShareAt`,
Honest/Law/RowDebtsAtByKind.lean, whose fields are pays · bud · on; another house's) at G :=
`theGOfReturn` made h T K, K := `theK` E apart (`laterOurs` A h.head) (E2E/TheKOfRecord.lean;
AtFullSide/M1/KRecord.lean: other houses' files), at every E, apart, T, Ry and Th. No definition;
two statements.

  `k12_pays_at_theK`   `KindPays` G .K12 at that G: another house's `kindPays_K12_theG`
      (AtFullSide/M1/K12AtK.lean) at that K, carried to the description that the return holds by
      `castSides_of`. From made · h · apart · slot₁₂. That house's own `theK_pays_four_ofReturn`
      gives the same clause beside three other kinds', under the live test and three more
      equations on E, which this kind's clause does not read. Its binder on the scope is not taken
      here either, BUT THE SCOPE IS READ: it is a field of h.head (`AtMg`.scope), and
      `noneSpent_at_maker` spends it. Both statements take h, so neither speaks of files outside
      the scope.
  `k12_share_at_theK_from_the_first_and_last_chains`   `k12_share_at_theK`
      (AtFullSide/K12/MembershipsAtTheK.lean) with its premise pays paid by the first statement.

THE PREMISES THAT STAY, SORTED. THE MAKER AND THE HEAD: made · h. ON E: apart · slot₁₂. THE FIRST
CHAIN's TEST: on₁ (another house's share). THE REQUEST's OWN TEST: hM · left₃.

WHAT pays SAYS. In `KindPays` the letter A' under "there are" is taken by the laws called as
"never" (AtFullSide/M1/K12Closed.lean's Limits: "`Good` at A := False: `plays` and `acc` are met
for nothing, and `exact` is conditional on On"); B' likewise, and idle there. fresh is met at an
empty list: by `noneSpent_at_maker` nothing is spent OF a part of this kind, so as an owner the
kind owes nothing. What bears weight in pays is fits, and exact at the list's own On and bud.

Every letter under "there are". In the first end: A', B' of `KindPays`: tied to nothing by that
definition; taken as above. In left₃ (a hypothesis): Th₃ and Said are tied to the family by one
equation, at border 2 alone; inside it `OwnTestDebts`.thread holds further letters, tied to Th₃ by
one HEq (AtFullSide/K12/SecondShareK12.lean's head). M is bound by "for all" and tied by hM.

WHAT A REVIEWER ASKS BESIDE A SHARE, AND WHERE IT STANDS HERE. (a) No premise but memberships in K:
NOT MET: on₁, hM, left₃ stand beside apart and slot₁₂. (b) "Bear": NOT TYPED AT theK: the three
laws are general in K (`k12_rows_theG`, AtFullSide/M1/KindRowsTheG.lean;
`k12_hrows_at_theGOfReturn`, AtFullSide/K12/SharedShareAtTheGOfReturn.lean;
`k12_hrows₃_at_theGOfReturn`, AtFullSide/K12/ShareK12.lean) under hK₀ and hK₁ to hK₄, which
AtFullSide/K12/MembershipsAtTheK.lean pays at theK; no statement joins them. (c) "Stands": THAT THE
FOUR LISTS STAND IN G WITH A SIDE IS TYPED NOWHERE HERE. (d) THREE OF THE FOUR TESTS SPEND (the
test on G_omega does not): `exact` draws the spent blocks anew. At a run they are not new: the
condition that answers for it is `fresh` on their owners' lists, in the pays of the owners' kinds
(K2; K1), NOT HERE, and the rule that joins fresh to exact is not here either. The owners:
AtFullSide/K12/ShareK12.lean's head, (d) [another house's count; not read].

THE LABEL "NOT IN FRONT OF A LAW OVER COINS" (the rule: Johnson/Bind/ForProver/FiveFieldsAt.lean's
head). The second statement calls `k12_share_at_theK`, which calls the gather, which calls
`k12_on₃_at_base` (AtFullSide/K12/SecondShareK12.lean), which calls `onAtRun_W_six_paid`
(Sim2/ListWSixPaid.lean), which bears it. OUR READING, WHICH IS NO RULING, as at
AtFullSide/K12/MembershipsAtTheK.lean's head: it is not inherited here. The letters that stay: Th,
M, Ry, with a thread and a companion under "there are" in left₃. on₁ and left₃ bind the committer's
randomness and the run's coins by "for all" inside the premise, and hM names no coin. Ry is of the
rule's second kind: it narrows the inputs, and a law in front of which the term stands has to name
it.

WHAT IT IS NOT. Not the row at the names of record: E, apart, T and Th are letters, and the
relation is `K12Rel` files Ry at a letter Ry.

Limits. FIRST the limit on the committer's randomness at the test on G_u
(AtFullSide/K12/OnAtRunUAtCommittersKey.lean's head, as AtFullSide/K12/ShareK12.lean's Limits put
it: the row binds the input first and ranges then over the lent coins and the challenges alone).
All limits of the files called. At the base filling, not at the filling that the online prover
reads. Other houses' values (`laterOurs`, `theK`) may turn, and then this file turns with them.
Nothing on completeness, soundness or hiding.
No property of the protocol is claimed.
-/
import AtFullSide.K12.MembershipsAtTheK
import AtFullSide.M1.K12AtK

